rem ACMP 304 - Volleyball 2 (Волейбол - 2)
rem Solved in Euler 1-15 style with exact combinatorial ballot counting.
rem
rem We want to count the number of point-by-point trajectories for a volleyball match.
rem Each set is played to Target points (25 for sets 1..4, 15 for set 5) with a lead of >= 2.
rem
rem For a set with final score A : B (assume A > B):
rem   1. Normal win (A == Target, B <= Target - 2):
rem      The winner scores the final point. All previous (A - 1) points of winner
rem      and B points of loser can appear in any order:
rem        Ways = C((A - 1) + B, B) = C(A + B - 1, B)
rem   2. Overtime / deuce (A > Target, A == B + 2):
rem      The game must reach (Target - 1) : (Target - 1), requiring C(2T, T) ways.
rem      Each subsequent tie (T+i):(T+i) offers exactly 2 point-pair choices ((1,2) or (2,1)),
rem      followed by 2 consecutive points for the winner:
rem        Ways = C(2T, T) * 2^(B - T)
rem
rem Total ways for the match is the product of the ways of all N sets.

use io
use cli
use sequences
use text
use numbers
use bits

arg N integer = 3
arg MatchesText text = "25:23 25:20 25:18"

Tokens = (MatchesText words) integer
TotalWays = 1

for SIdx in 0 till N
  A = Tokens (2 * SIdx)
  B = Tokens (2 * SIdx + 1)

  Target = 25
  if SIdx equal 4
    Target = 15
  end
  T = Target - 1

  MaxScore = A max B
  MinScore = A min B
  SetWays = 0

  if (MaxScore equal Target) and (not (MinScore greater (Target - 2)))
    SetWays = (MaxScore + MinScore - 1) binomial MinScore
  else
    BaseWays = (2 * T) binomial T
    Power = 1 shl (MinScore - T)
    SetWays = BaseWays * Power
  end

  TotalWays = TotalWays * SetWays
end

Answer = TotalWays
Answer print
